# Keeps `public/` in the repository although it is empty.
#
# WHY AN EMPTY DIRECTORY IS LOAD-BEARING
# ======================================
# `next build` with `output: "standalone"` does NOT copy `public/` into
# `.next/standalone`, so the production image has to copy it separately --
# infra/docker/web.Dockerfile does exactly that. Docker's COPY fails the build when
# its source does not exist, and git does not track empty directories, so without
# this file the image build fails with:
#
#   "/repo/apps/web/public": not found
#
# which is what happened the first time CI actually ran the docker job.
#
# The alternative was to delete the COPY line. That would work today and break the
# day somebody adds a favicon: the file would be committed, served in development,
# and silently missing in production. An empty directory is the cheaper mistake.
#
# Anything dropped in here is served from the site root, publicly and unauthenticated.
# Never put evidence artifacts or anything reviewer-specific here.
